#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid "'very' Bloody Mary cocktail"
msgid_plural "'very' Bloody Mary cocktail"
msgstr[0] "cóctel \"muy\" Bloody Mary"
msgstr[1] "cócteles \"muy\" Bloody Mary"
msgstr[2] "cócteles \"muy\" Bloody Mary"

#. ~ Description of "nigori sake"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A Japanese alcoholic beverage made by fermenting rice with the use of yeast "
"and koji mold.  This one has a cloudy white color because of fine rice "
"particles in it, as it has not been filtered."
msgstr ""
"Bebida alcohólica japonesa elaborada mediante la fermentación del arroz con "
"el uso de levadura y moho koji. Este tiene un color blanco turbio debido a "
"las finas partículas de arroz que contiene, ya que no ha sido filtrado."

#. ~ Description of "sake"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A Japanese alcoholic beverage made by fermenting rice with the use of yeast "
"and koji mold.  This one is mostly clear, as it has been filtered."
msgstr ""
"Bebida alcohólica japonesa elaborada mediante la fermentación del arroz con "
"el uso de levadura y moho koji. Esta es mayormente clara, ya que ha sido "
"filtrada."

#. ~ Description of "vodka"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A beverage of alcohol, water, and not much else.  In America, men make "
"vodka, but in Soviet Russia, vodka makes the man."
msgstr ""
"Una bebida de alcohol, agua, y no mucho más. En América, los hombres hacen "
"vodka, pero en la Rusia soviética, el vodka hace al hombre."

#. ~ Description of "Long Island iced tea"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A blend of incredibly strong-flavored liquors that somehow tastes like none "
"of them.  It contains no tea, but the inclusion of cola gives it a tea-like "
"color."
msgstr ""
"Una mezcla de licores de sabor increíble y fuerte, que de alguna manera, "
"termina no teniendo el gusto de ninguno de ellos. No contiene te, pero la "
"inclusión de bebida de cola le da ese color parecido al té."

#. ~ Description of "pina colada"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A cocktail consisting of pineapple juice, coconut milk, and rum, originating "
"in Puerto Rico.  In certain variants, vodka, whiskey, or tequila are "
"substituted for rum."
msgstr ""
"Cóctel compuesto por zumo de piña, leche de coco y ron, originario de Puerto "
"Rico. En algunas variantes, el ron se sustituye por vodka, whisky o tequila."

#. ~ Description of "tequila sunrise"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A cocktail consisting of tequila, orange juice, and grenadine syrup, "
"originating from California.  In certain variants, vodka or rum may be "
"substituted for tequila, and pineapple juice may be substituted for orange "
"juice."
msgstr ""
"Cóctel compuesto por tequila, zumo de naranja y jarabe de granadina, "
"originario de California. En algunas variantes, el tequila puede sustituirse "
"por vodka o ron, y el zumo de piña por zumo de naranja."

#. ~ Description of "Queen Mary cocktail"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid "A cocktail made by mixing beer and grenadine syrup.  It's quite sweet."
msgstr ""
"Un cóctel elaborado con la mezcla de cerveza y jarabe de granadina. Es "
"bastante dulce."

#. ~ Description of "gunfire cocktail"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A cocktail made by mixing black tea and rum, which has its origins in the "
"British Army."
msgstr ""
"Un cóctel elaborado mediante la mezcla de té negro y ron, que tiene su "
"origen en el ejército británico."

#. ~ Description of "karsk"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A cocktail made by mixing coffee and pure alcohol, typically moonshine, "
"originating from Scandinavia."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "tequila"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A distilled alcoholic beverage made from a succulent plant with spiky "
"leaves.  Don't eat the worm!  Wait, there's no worm in this bottle."
msgstr ""
"Una bebida alcohólica destilada hecha de una planta suculenta con hojas "
"espinosas. ¡No te comas el gusano! Espera, no hay ningún gusano en esta "
"botella."

#. ~ Description of "rum"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A distilled alcoholic beverage made from fermenting molasses.  Drinking it "
"might make you feel like a pirate.  Or not."
msgstr ""
"Una bebida alcohólica destilada hecha de melaza fermentada. Beberla puede "
"hacerte sentir como un pirata. O no."

#. ~ Description of "whiskey"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A distilled grain alcohol, made from, by, and for real Southern colonels!"
msgstr ""
"¡Un alcohol de grano destilado, hecho desde, por y para verdaderos coroneles "
"sureños!"

#. ~ Description of "Bristol Cream"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A fine sherry that has been aged in American oak casks and bottled in "
"Bristol, England."
msgstr ""
"Un fino jerez que ha sido envejecido en barriles de roble americano y "
"embotellado en Bristol, Inglaterra."

#. ~ Description of "Belgian ale"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A flavorful and filling beer brewed by monks in Belgium.  Best served in a "
"goblet."
msgstr ""
"Una cerveza sabrosa y que llena elaborada por monjes en Bélgica. Se sirve "
"mejor en un cáliz."

#. ~ Description of "beer"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A generic-brand grain alcohol flavored with hops.  It's best served cold, in "
"a glass, and with a lime - but you're not that lucky."
msgstr ""
"Un alcohol de grano de marca genérica aromatizado con lúpulo. Se sirve mejor "
"frío, en un vaso y con una lima, pero no tienes tanta suerte."

#. ~ Description of "European pilsner"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A lager beer imported from Europe.  Best served cold, in a glass - but "
"you're not that lucky."
msgstr ""
"Una cerveza lager importada de Europa. Se sirve mejor fría, en vaso de "
"cristal... pero no tienes tanta suerte."

#. ~ Description of "burdock wine"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid "A light and delicious wine made from burdock roots.  Somewhat sweet."
msgstr "Un ligero y delicioso vino hecho de raíces de bardana. Algo dulce."

#. ~ Description of "dandelion wine"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A light and delicious wine made from dandelion flowers.  Slightly "
"effervescent, it is smooth and crisp."
msgstr ""
"Un vino liviano y delicioso hecho con flores de diente de león. Ligeramente "
"efervescente, suave y fresco."

#. ~ Description of "kalimotxo"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A mix of equal parts wine and cola, originating in Spain in the 1920s.  "
"Tastes better than it sounds."
msgstr ""
"Una mezcla de vino y cola a partes iguales, originada en España en la década "
"de 1920. Sabe mejor de lo que parece."

#. ~ Description of "screwdriver cocktail"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A mix of orange juice and vodka.  It's the surreptitious drunkard mechanic's "
"drink of choice.  A similar drink may be made by substituting cranberry "
"juice for orange juice."
msgstr ""
"Una mezcla de zumo de naranja y vodka. Es la bebida preferida de los "
"mecánicos borrachos subrepticios. Se puede hacer una bebida similar "
"sustituyendo el zumo de naranja por zumo de arándanos."

#. ~ Description of "gin and tonic"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A mixed alcoholic drink consisting of gin and tonic water, created in the "
"19th century as a way to make tonic water (a malaria prophylactic) more "
"palatable, but still popular to this day.  In certain variants, vodka is "
"substituted for gin."
msgstr ""
"Bebida alcohólica mixta compuesta por ginebra y agua tónica, creada en el "
"siglo XIX como forma de hacer más apetecible el agua tónica (un profiláctico "
"de la malaria), pero que sigue siendo popular en la actualidad. En algunas "
"variantes, la ginebra se sustituye por vodka."

#. ~ Description of "honeygold brew"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A mixed drink combining bee and ant honey.  It tastes great, and it's a good "
"source of nourishment."
msgstr ""
"Una bebida mixta que combina miel de abeja y de hormiga. Sabe muy bien y es "
"una buena fuente de alimento."

#. ~ Description of "whiskey sour"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A mixed drink made of whiskey and lemon juice, with sugar added.  In certain "
"variants, gin is substituted for whiskey."
msgstr ""
"Bebida mixta elaborada con whisky y zumo de limón, a la que se añade azúcar. "
"En algunas variantes, el whisky se sustituye por ginebra."

#. ~ Description of "Canadian whiskey"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid "A multi-grain liquor made from a mash of corn and rye."
msgstr "Un licor multigrano hecho de un puré de maíz y centeno."

#. ~ Description of "martini"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A popular cocktail made with gin and dry vermouth, dating from the "
"Prohibition era.  In certain variants, vodka or tequila is substituted for "
"gin."
msgstr ""
"Cóctel popular elaborado con ginebra y vermut seco, que data de la época de "
"la Prohibición. En algunas variantes, la ginebra se sustituye por vodka o "
"tequila."

#. ~ Description of "pine wine"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A potent wine flavored with pine resin.  Bold and pungent, its biting taste "
"and strong aroma takes some getting used to."
msgstr ""
"Un potente vino con gusto a resina de pino. Intenso y áspero, por su sabor "
"mordaz y aroma fuerte. Cuesta acostumbrarse a él."

#. ~ Description of "vermouth"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A soft wine with a pleasant herbal flavor and aroma.  It is a common "
"cocktail ingredient, and can be used as a substitute for white wine."
msgstr ""
"Un vino suave con un agradable sabor y aroma a hierbas. Es un ingrediente "
"común en los cócteles, y puede ser usado como sustituto del vino blanco."

#. ~ Description of "stout"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid "A tasty craft beer, as dark in color as the days ahead."
msgstr ""
"Una sabrosa cerveza artesanal, tan negra de color como los días futuros."

#. ~ Description of "American pale ale"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A tasty domestic craft beer.  Best served cold, in a glass - but you're not "
"that lucky."
msgstr ""
"Una sabrosa cerveza artesanal nacional. Se sirve mejor fría, en un vaso - "
"pero no tienes tanta suerte."

#. ~ Description of "imperial stout"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A very flavorful beer that has been aged in bourbon barrels.  It is as black "
"as midnight on a moonless night and has the viscosity of oil.  While very "
"tasty, it also has an alcohol content on par with wine."
msgstr ""
"Una cerveza muy sabrosa que ha sido envejecida en barriles de bourbon. Es "
"tan negra como la medianoche en una noche sin luna y tiene la viscosidad del "
"aceite. Aunque es muy sabrosa, también tiene una graduación alcohólica a la "
"altura del vino."

#. ~ Description of "India pale ale"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"A very flavorful microbrewed beer.  Best served cold, in a glass - but "
"you're not that lucky."
msgstr ""
"Una cerveza elaborada con mucho sabor. Se sirve mejor fría, en vaso de "
"cristal... pero no tienes tanta suerte."

#. ~ Description of "Marloss wine"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid "A viscous, soft pink wine, made from the fruit of the Marloss."
msgstr "Es un vino viscoso y rosa clarito hecho con la fruta del Marloss."

#. ~ Description of "single pot still Irish whiskey"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid "A whiskey made from a mixed mash of malted and unmalted barley."
msgstr "Un whisky hecho con una mezcla de cebada malteada y no malteada."

#. ~ Description of "marsala"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid "A wine popularly used in dishes served in Italian restaurants."
msgstr ""
"Un vino usado popularmente en los platos que se sirven en los restaurantes "
"italianos."

#. ~ Description of "hard seltzer"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"Alcoholic sparkling water infused with delicious fruit.  Perfect for a hot "
"summer day."
msgstr ""
"Agua gaseosa mezclada con deliciosa fruta.  Perfecta para un día caluroso de "
"verano."

#. ~ Description of "homebrew hard seltzer"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"Alcoholic sparkling water infused with delicious fruit.  Perfect for a hot "
"summer day.  Tastes nearly as good as the one in the market."
msgstr ""
"Agua gaseosa mezclada con deliciosa fruta.  Perfecta para un día caluroso de "
"verano.  Sabe casi igual que la comprada en el mercado."

#. ~ Description of "Chardonnay"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid "America's most popular wine, and for good reason."
msgstr "El vino más popular de Estados Unidos, y con razón."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid "American pale ale"
msgid_plural "American pale ale"
msgstr[0] "Pale ale americana"
msgstr[1] "Pale ale americana"
msgstr[2] "Pale ale americana"

#. ~ Description of "gin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid ""
"An alcoholic beverage flavored with juniper berries.  It smells faintly of "
"berries, but mostly booze."
msgstr ""
"Es una bebida con alcohol con gusto a bayas de enebro. Tiene un débil aroma "
"a baya, y más que nada a alcohol."

#. ~ Description of "triple sec"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/alcohol.json
msgid "An orange-flavored liquor used in many mixed drinks."
msgstr "Un licor con gusto a naranja que se usa en muchos bebidas."

