#. ~ Description of variant "AK bayonet"of gun mod "Bayonet"
#. ~ Description of variant "AK bayonet" of item "Bayonet"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A 6H4 bayonet for Kalashnikov pattern rifles, usually imported military "
"surplus from eastern bloc countries.  The blade is made of stainless steel "
"and the handle of a lightweight and durable plastic.  It features a middling "
"metal saw on the spine of the blade, and can function as a wire cutter as "
"well.  Though it is quite sturdy, it can't hold an edge very well."
msgstr ""
"Un bayoneta 6H4 para rifles de patrón Kalashnikov, generalmente importados "
"como excedentes militares de países del bloque del este. La hoja está hecha "
"de acero inoxidable y el mango de un plástico ligero y duradero. Cuenta con "
"una sierra de metal mediana en el lomo de la hoja y también puede funcionar "
"como un cortador de alambre. Aunque es bastante resistente, no puede "
"mantener un filo muy bien."

#. ~ Description of gun mod "National Guard bayonet"
#. ~ Description of "National Guard bayonet"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A Cold War era Army bayonet that has only partially been replaced by newer "
"models.  It has an apocalypse-proof full-tang, double-edged high steel blade "
"terminating in a spear point.  The no-frills design makes for both a good "
"fighting knife and bayonet, a fact that was appreciated when reserve stocks "
"of these were issued out to National Guardsmen."
msgstr ""
"Una bayoneta del ejército de la guerra fría que ha sido parcialmente "
"reemplazada por modelos más nuevos. Tiene una espiga a prueba de "
"apocalipsis, hoja de acero alto en carbono de doble filo que acaba en una "
"punta de lanza. Su sencillo diseño lo convierte en un buen cuchillo de "
"combate y bayoneta, un hecho que fue apreciado cuando las reservas "
"almacenadas de estas fueron entregadas a la Guardia Nacional."

#. ~ Description of "bronze knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A cast bronze knife with a full tang, with a handle wrapped in cord and "
"leather, work-hardened and sharpened to a fine edge."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "kirpan"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A ceremonial dagger carried by Sikh men.  This one is sharp and could be an "
"effective weapon."
msgstr ""
"Una daga ceremonial llevada por hombres Sikh. Esta es afilada y podría ser "
"un arma efectiva."

#. ~ Description of "bone shiv"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A femur or other bone, about 20 cm long, which has been broken at one end "
"and sharpened into a cutting tool.  Its jagged edge is wicked but fragile."
msgstr ""
"Un fémur u otro hueso, de unos 20 cm de longitud, que se ha roto por un "
"extremo y se ha afilado como herramienta de corte. Su borde dentado es "
"malvado pero frágil."

#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "survival knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid "A hidden handle compartment.  Unscrew the compass to access."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "makeshift knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A knife consisting of a long, somewhat sharpened spike and a tightly-wrapped "
"rag as a handle.  Not as good as a real knife, but it'll do in a pinch."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo que consiste en una punta larga más o menos afilada, y un trapo "
"fuertemente enrollado que funciona como empuñadura. No es como un cuchillo "
"de servirá en un apuro."

#. ~ Description of "copper knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A knife made of crudely-worked copper with a simple handle.  Primitive, but "
"a step above stone-age."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo que consiste en cobre trabajado toscamente, y un agarre simple. "
"Primitivo, pero un paso más adelante de la edad de piedra."

#. ~ Description of "poignard"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A long, slim knife from the Renaissance era associated with knighthood, "
"nobility, and warriors of Safavid Iran, these blades were as much a status "
"symbol as an elegant tool for slipping through the gaps in metal armor."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "switchblade"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A long, thin knife with a spring-loaded blade that rests inside the handle "
"while not in use."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo largo y fino con una hoja que se oculta dentro de la empuñadura "
"cuando no está en uso y sale por la acción de un resorte."

#. ~ Description of "carving knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A long-bladed kitchen knife with a thin, slightly curved blade for deftly "
"slicing meat either in flat sheets or around the bone.  It makes a decent "
"melee weapon, and is excellent for butchery."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo de cocina de hoja larga, fina y curva para poder cortar carne en "
"filetes o para deshuesar. Es un arma decente para el c. a c. pero es "
"excelente para descuartizado."

#. ~ Description of "chef knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A long-bladed kitchen knife.  The blade is wider than the handle, giving "
"room for the wielder's knuckles, and it has a characteristic curve for a "
"fast rocking action for chopping vegetables.  It makes an acceptable melee "
"weapon, but the wide blade is unwieldy for butchering."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo de cocina con una hoja larga. La hoja es más ancha que la "
"empuñadura, tiene espacio para los nudillos y una curva característica que "
"permite cortar verduras a gran velocidad. Como arma de c. a c. funciona "
"aceptablemente pero la cuchilla ancha es un poco incómoda para descuartizar."

#. ~ Description of "baselard"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A medieval dagger forged from rough iron.  It is not the sharpest tool in "
"the shed, but it is certainly one of the largest."
msgstr ""
"Una daga medieval forjada con hierro en bruto. No es la herramienta más "
"afilada del almacén, pero sin duda es una de las más grandes."

#. ~ Description of "vegetable cleaver"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A menacing-looking knife with a broad, square shaped blade, curved for fast "
"vegetable chopping.  Its heft and sharpness make it a decent weapon as well, "
"although not as good as a meat cleaver."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo de aspecto amenazante con una hoja ancha, medio cuadrada y curva "
"para cortar verduras de manera rápida. Su peso y filo la convierten en una "
"decente arma de c. a c. aunque no tan buena como una cuchilla de carnicero."

#. ~ Description of "meat cleaver"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A menacing-looking knife with a broad, square-shaped blade.  Its heft and "
"sharpness would make it a very effective melee weapon and an excellent "
"butchering tool."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo de aspecto amenazante con una hoja ancha, medio cuadrada y "
"curva. Su peso y filo la convierten en un arma de c. a c. muy efectiva, y "
"una excelente herramienta para descuartizar."

#. ~ Description of gun mod "USMC bayonet"
#. ~ Description of "USMC bayonet"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A modern bayonet in use with the US Marine Corps, adopted in an effort to "
"improve USMC hand-to-hand fighting capabilities.  The bayonet is optimized "
"to function as a fighting knife, sporting an ergonomic handle that will "
"minimize hand fatigue during combat.  The blade tip is sharper in profile "
"than other bayonets to assist in penetrating body armor, and also features a "
"small serrated section to provide for some utility."
msgstr ""
"Una bayoneta moderna en uso por el Cuerpo de Marines de USA, adoptada en un "
"esfuerzo por mejorar las capacidades de combate c.a.c USMC. La bayoneta está "
"optimizada para funcionar como cuchillo de combate, con un mango ergonómico "
"que minimiza la fatiga en la mano durante el combate. La punta de la hoja "
"está más afilada que otras bayonetas para asistir en la penetración de "
"armaduras corporales, y también tiene una pequeña sección serrada para otros "
"usos."

#. ~ Description of "stone chopper"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A rock with sharpened edges, produced by knapping.  Works as a crude cutting "
"and butchering tool, if nothing else is available."
msgstr ""
"Una roca con bordes afilados, producida por el golpeo. Sirve como "
"herramienta de corte y descuartizado, si no se dispone de otra cosa."

#. ~ Description of "steak knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A sharp knife designed for cutting meat.  It makes a poor melee weapon, but "
"is decent at butchering corpses."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo afilado diseñado para cortar carne. No sirve mucho como arma de "
"cuerpo a cuerpo pero es decente para descuartizar cadáveres."

#. ~ Description of "butcher knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A sharp, heavy knife.  It makes a good melee weapon, and is an ideal item "
"for butchering corpses."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo grande y afilado. Sirve bien como arma de c. a c. y es ideal "
"para descuartizar cadáveres."

#. ~ Description of "honey scraper"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A sharp, knife-like tool used for harvesting honey from beehives.  Makes a "
"passable melee weapon."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta afilada parecida a un cuchillo, que se usa para sacar la "
"miel de las colmenas. También puede servir como arma c. a c."

#. ~ Description of "stone knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A sharpened stone set into a hollowed handle.  Not nearly as usable as a "
"proper knife, but it's better than nothing."
msgstr ""
"Una piedra afilada puesta dentro de un mango ahuecado. No es ni por asomo "
"tan útil como un cuchillo serio, pero es mejor que nada."

#. ~ Description of "dive knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A short, sturdy knife with a serrated edge for cutting lines and straps, and "
"a blunt tip for prying.  Used primarily by divers, this knife has been "
"fitted with cork to slow its descent if dropped underwater, so it takes up "
"more space than usual."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo corto y robusto con un filo dentado para cortar cabos, correas, "
"y una punta roma para hacer palanca. Utilizado principalmente por los "
"buceadores, este cuchillo ha sido dotado de corcho para ralentizar su "
"descenso si se deja caer bajo el agua, por lo que ocupa más espacio de lo "
"habitual."

#. ~ Description of "paring knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A short-bladed knife with a sharp blade, made for fine controlled cuts to "
"vegetables without using a cutting board."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo de hoja corta con un filo afilado, hecho para cortes finos y "
"controlados de vegetales sin usar una tabla de cortar."

#. ~ Description of "folding knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A small folding knife with a locking blade and a pocket clip.  Not as good a "
"weapon as a solid fixed-blade knife, but better than a penknife."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño cuchillo plegable, con traba para la hoja y gancho para colgarlo "
"del cinto. No es tan buen arma como los que tienen cuchilla fija pero es "
"mejor que una navaja."

#. ~ Description of "boxcutter knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A small knife designed for opening boxes.  It could cause some damage, but "
"it really should be used against inanimate objects.  It is too small to "
"effectively butcher corpses with."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo pequeño, diseñado para abrir cajas. Puede causar algo de daño, "
"pero en realidad debería usarse contra objetos inanimados. Es demasiado "
"pequeño para descuartizar cadáveres."

#. ~ Description of "pocket knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A small pocket knife.  It isn't great for combat, but it's better than "
"nothing.  It's sharp enough to butcher with."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña navaja de bolsillo. No es muy útil en combate, pero es mejor que "
"nada. Y es bastante afilada como para usarla para descuartizar."

#. ~ Description of "karambit"
#: data/json/items/melee/short_blades.json
msgid ""
"A traditional Indonesian knife.  The blade is very short, but its curved "
"design is perfect for precision attacks."
msgstr ""

