#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
msgid ""
"Damn right.  They lied to us for god knows how long about what was going on "
"because they didn't want us to figure it out.  It probably started as a way "
"to keep the people in line, but it backfired somehow.  My guess is they "
"tried to de-educate us, tried to mislead us, and when that wasn't working "
"they tried actual drugs in the water to make us stupid or something.  "
"Instead of just stupid, some people got violent.  Then they tried to "
"leverage that to put in martial law, but that didn't work and they wound up "
"fighting hordes of people.  Only they didn't realize their <swear> brain "
"drugs were some kind of mutagen that turn people into zombies."
msgstr ""
"Malditamente cierto. Nos mintieron durante Dios sabe cuánto tiempo sobre lo "
"que estaba pasando porque no querían que lo descubriéramos. Probablemente "
"comenzó como una forma de mantener a la gente a raya, pero de alguna manera "
"les salió el tiro por la culata. Mi opinión es que intentaron deseducarnos, "
"trataron de engañarnos y, cuando eso no funcionó, probaron con drogas reales "
"en el agua para volvernos estúpidos o algo así. En lugar de ser estúpidos, "
"algunos se volvieron violentos. Luego trataron de aprovechar eso para poner "
"la ley marcial, pero eso no funcionó y terminaron luchando contra hordas de "
"personas. Sólo que no se dieron cuenta de que sus <swear> drogas cerebrales "
"eran una especie de mutágeno que convertía a la gente en zombis."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
msgid "How did you get out?"
msgstr "¿Cómo saliste?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
msgid ""
"I think it's mostly mutation.  I don't know what they used, but it's some "
"real mad science shit, I didn't think most of this was even possible.  I "
"also wonder if whatever they put in the water has made us a bit crazy.  "
"Maybe some of this is just a hallucination?  That one blows my mind a bit, "
"I'm not sure I believe it but I got nothin' else."
msgstr ""
"Creo que es mayormente una mutación. No sé lo que usaron, pero es una "
"verdadera mierda de ciencia loca, no pensé que la mayoría de esto fuera "
"posible. También me pregunto si lo que pusieron en el agua nos ha vuelto un "
"poco locos. ¿Tal vez algo de esto es sólo una alucinación? Eso me vuelve "
"loco, no estoy seguro de creerlo pero no tengo ninguna otra idea."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
msgid ""
"It was terrifying.  We were shipped there on a repurposed school bus, about "
"thirty of us.  You can probably see the issues right away.  A few of the "
"folks on board the bus had injuries, and some schmuck who had seen too many "
"B-movies tried to insist that anyone who 'had been bitten' was going to "
"'turn'.  Fucking idiot, right?  I've been bitten a dozen times now and the "
"worst I got was a gross infection."
msgstr ""
"Fue aterrador. Nos enviaron allí en un autobús escolar modificado, unos "
"treinta de nosotros. Probablemente puedas ver los problemas de inmediato. "
"Algunos de los que iban a bordo del autobús tenían heridas, y algún imbécil "
"que había visto demasiadas películas de serie B trató de insistir en que "
"cualquiera que \"hubiera sido mordido\" iba a \"convertirse'\". Maldito "
"idiota, ¿verdad? Me han mordido una docena de veces y lo peor que he tenido "
"ha sido una grave infección."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
msgid "Maybe another time.  I don't really like thinking about it."
msgstr "Tal vez en otro momento. No me gusta mucho pensar en ello."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
msgid "Oh?"
msgstr "¿Oh?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
msgid "Sorry for asking.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Perdón por preguntar. <done_conversation_section>"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
msgid "Sorry for asking.  <end_talking>"
msgstr "Perdón por preguntar ¡.  <end_talking>"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
msgid "Sorry.  Tell me more about that FEMA camp."
msgstr "Lo siento. Cuéntame más sobre el campamento de la FEMA."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
msgid "Tell me more about that FEMA camp."
msgstr "Cuéntame más sobre ese campamento del FEMA."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
msgid ""
"That guy started a frenzy.  People were already panicked.  There was an "
"armed guy overseeing the transport, acting like a cop but really he was just "
"some <dumb> kid they'd handed a rifle to.  He tried to calm things down, and "
"I guess it actually worked for a bit, although the 'kill the infected' bunch "
"were pretty <swear> freaked out and were clearly ready to jump the moment "
"the granny with the cut on her arm started frothing at the mouth.  They "
"started acting up again when we got to the camp.  That didn't go well for "
"them.  A few heavily armed soldiers dragged them away, and I never saw them "
"again."
msgstr ""
"Ese tipo se puso frenético. La gente ya estaba en pánico. Había un tipo "
"armado supervisando el transporte, actuando como un policía pero en realidad "
"era sólo un <dumb>chico al que le habían dado un rifle. Intentó calmar las "
"cosas, y supongo que funcionó por un tiempo, aunque los del grupo de \"matar "
"a los infectados\" estaban bastante <swear>asustados y estaban claramente "
"listos para saltar en el momento en que la abuelita con el corte en el brazo "
"empezara a echar espuma por la boca. Comenzaron a actuar de nuevo cuando "
"llegamos al campamento. Eso no les fue bien. Unos pocos soldados fuertemente "
"armados los arrastraron, y nunca los volví a ver."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid ""
"That place was chaos.  I only stayed a few hours.  They had a big backhoe "
"running, digging a huge pit in a cordoned section they wouldn't let us "
"near.  Well, I managed to sneak over that way, and saw them dumping load "
"after load of the dead in the pit, pouring dirt back over them even as they "
"revived and tried to climb out.  Even with all the shit I've seen since, it "
"haunts me.  I knew then I had to get out.  Luckily for me, we were attacked "
"the next morning by some giant horror, a kind I haven't really seen since "
"then.  While the guards were busy with that, I grabbed some supplies I'd "
"stocked up over the night and I fucked right out of there.  A few others "
"tried to fuck out with me, but as far as I know I was the only lucky one."
msgstr ""
"Ese lugar era un caos. Sólo me quedé unas pocas horas. Tenían una gran "
"retroexcavadora corriendo, cavando un enorme hoyo en una sección acordonada "
"a la que no nos dejaban acercarnos. Me las arreglé para escabullirme por "
"ahí, y los vi arrojando carga tras carga de muertos en la fosa, echándoles "
"tierra encima incluso cuando revivían e intentaban salir. Incluso con toda "
"la mierda que he visto desde entonces, esa imagen me persigue. Supe entonces "
"que tenía que salir. Por suerte para mí, fuimos atacados a la mañana "
"siguiente por un horror gigante, un tipo que no he visto desde entonces. "
"Mientras los guardias estaban ocupados con eso, agarré algunas provisiones "
"que había almacenado durante la noche y me fui a tomar por culo de allí. "
"Algunos otros trataron de joderme , pero hasta donde sé, yo fui el único "
"afortunado."

