#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
msgid "No.  I can't.  Just, no."
msgstr "No. No puedo. Simplemente, no."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid ""
"Somehow, I don't know how, I managed to fall asleep in there.  I think it "
"might have started with me hyperventilating and passing out.  When I woke up "
"it was night, I was starving and parched, and… and the screaming had died "
"down.  At first I tried to go out the way I came in, but I peaked out the "
"window and saw one of the nurses stumbling around, spitting that black shit "
"up.  Her name was Becky.  She wasn't Becky anymore.  So, I went back up and "
"somehow made it into the storage area.  From there, the roof.  I drank water "
"from some nasty old puddle and I camped out there for a while, watching the "
"city around me burn."
msgstr ""
"De alguna manera, no sé cómo, me las arreglé para quedarme dormido allí. "
"Creo que podría haber empezado conmigo hiperventilando y desmayándome. "
"Cuando me desperté, era de noche y estaba muerto de sed y hambre, y... y los "
"gritos se habían calmado. Al principio intenté salir por donde había "
"entrado, pero echo un vistazo por la ventana y vi a una de las enfermeras "
"tropezar, escupiendo esa mierda negra. Se llamaba Becky. Eso ya no era "
"Becky. Así que volví a subir y de alguna manera llegué al área de "
"almacenamiento. Desde allí, al tejado. Bebí agua de un viejo y desagradable "
"charco y acampé allí un rato, viendo arder la ciudad a mi alrededor."

