#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
msgid "Sorry for changing the subject.  What was it you were saying?"
msgstr "Perdón por cambiar el tema. ¿Qué me estabas diciendo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
msgid "Sounds like it didn't work out."
msgstr "Suena como si no hubiera funcionado."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
msgid "Thanks for telling me that.  <end_talking>"
msgstr "Gracias por avisarme. <end_talking>"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
msgid "Thanks!  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "¡Gracias!  <done_conversation_section>"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
msgid "Thanks!  <end_talking>"
msgstr "¡Gracias! <end_talking>"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
msgid "Thanks!  What was it you were saying before?"
msgstr "¡Gracias! ¿Qué era lo que decías antes?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
msgid "Whatever's in that map benefits both of us."
msgstr "Lo que sea que esté en ese mapa nos beneficia a ambos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
msgid "Why did you leave your bunker?"
msgstr "¿Por qué dejaste el búnker?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, I do.  I'd be willing to part with them for, say, $1000.  Straight "
"from your ATM account, no cash cards."
msgstr ""
"Sí, lo sé. Estaría dispuesto a separarme de ellos por, digamos, 1000 "
"dólares. Directamente de tu cuenta de cajero automático, sin tarjetas de "
"crédito."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
msgid "[$1000] You have a deal."
msgstr "[$1000] Trato hecho."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
msgid ""
"Assault charges.  I really don't want to get into it, let's just say that "
"you don't want to talk during a movie around me okay?"
msgstr ""
"Cargos por asalto. No quiero entrar en eso, digamos que no querrás hablar "
"durante una película a mi alrededor, ¿vale?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
msgid "Did that actually work?"
msgstr "¿Funcionó realmente?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
msgid "How did you get out of lockup?"
msgstr "¿Cómo saliste del aislamiento?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
msgid ""
"I got a little bit into black market organ trading.  It sounds worse than it "
"was… but it was pretty bad."
msgstr ""
"Me metí un poco en el mercado negro de órganos. Suena peor de lo que era... "
"pero era bastante malo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid ""
"I heard gunshots, even from down in lockup.  Didn't hear much screaming or "
"anything.  That was my first clue something was up.  Food stopped showing "
"up, next.  Then, the lights went out.  I was down there for maybe hours, "
"maybe days, when finally a flashlight in the bars blinded me.  It was a "
"guard.  He let me out, filled me in on what was going on.  I wanted to think "
"he was crazy, but something in his eyes… I believed him."
msgstr ""
"Escuché disparos, incluso desde abajo, en el calabozo. No oí muchos gritos "
"ni nada. Esa fue mi primera pista de que algo estaba pasando. La comida dejó "
"de aparecer, la siguiente. Luego, las luces se apagaron. Estuve allí abajo "
"tal vez horas, tal vez días, cuando finalmente una linterna en los barrotes "
"me cegó. Era un guardia. Me dejó salir, me informó de lo que estaba pasando. "
"Quería pensar que estaba loco, pero algo en sus ojos... le creí."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
