#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
msgid ""
"Oh, yeah, this is a good choice.  Hold on to it for me, let's have a drink "
"later.  Right now we're practically swimming in good whisky, but some day "
"the last bottle will get drunk.  It's gonna be a long time before any of us "
"is brewing nice scotch, and we ain't never gettin' peat from Islay ever "
"again.  Makes me shed a tear just thinking about it."
msgstr ""
"Oh, sí, es una buena elección. Guárdalo por mí, tomemos un trago más tarde. "
"Ahora mismo estamos prácticamente nadando en buen whisky, pero algún día la "
"última botella se emborrachará. Va a pasar mucho tiempo antes de que alguno "
"de nosotros prepare un buen escocés, y no volveremos a recibir turba de "
"Islay nunca más. Me hace derramar una lágrima sólo de pensar en ello."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
msgid "Thanks for that.  Let's get going."
msgstr "Gracias por eso. Continuemos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
msgid "What was working for the Free Merchants like?"
msgstr "¿Cómo era trabajar para los Mercaderes Libres?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
msgid "What was working for the Old Guard like?"
msgstr "¿Y cómo era trabajar para la Vieja Guardia?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
msgid ""
"Why was a guy with your skillset guarding a warehouse?  Must've been some "
"warehouse."
msgstr ""
"¿Y qué hacía un tipo con tus habilidades cuidando un depósito? Debe haber "
"sido un depósito importante."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
msgid ""
"Why was someone with your skillset guarding a warehouse?  Must've been some "
"warehouse."
msgstr ""
"¿Por qué alguien con tus habilidades estaba vigilando un almacén? Debe haber "
"sido algún almacén."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, okay.  I can respect that.  How about this: bring me a bottle of "
"single malt, we share a drink, I tell you the story."
msgstr ""
"Sí, está bien. Puedo respetar eso. Qué te parece esto: tráeme una botella de "
"malta simple, compartimos un trago y te cuento la historia."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
msgid "You owe me a story."
msgstr "Me debes una historia."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scientist_1.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid ""
"Before <the_cataclysm> I worked in a lab.  Don't look at me like that, it "
"had nothing to do with this stuff… I was studying protein-protein "
"interactions in smooth muscle in mice, using NMR.  Nothing even vaguely "
"related to zombies.  Anyway, I was at last year's Experimental Biology "
"conference in San Francisco, and an old friend of mine was talking about "
"some really weird shit she'd heard of coming out of government labs.  Really "
"hush hush stuff.  Normally I wouldn't put much cred into that sort of thing, "
"but from her, it actually had me worried.  I packed a bug-out bag just in "
"case."
msgstr ""
"Antes del <the_cataclysm> que trabajara en un laboratorio. No me mires así, "
"no tenía nada que ver con esto... Estaba estudiando las interacciones "
"proteína-proteína en el músculo liso de los ratones, usando RMN. Nada que "
"esté vagamente relacionado con los zombis. De todos modos, estaba en la "
"conferencia de Biología Experimental del año pasado en San Francisco, y una "
"vieja amiga mía estaba hablando de una mierda muy rara que había oído de los "
"laboratorios del gobierno. Cosas realmente silenciosas. Normalmente no le "
"daría mucha credibilidad a ese tipo de cosas, pero de ella, me preocupaba. "
"Empaqué una mochila de escape por si acaso."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scientist_1.json
msgctxt "npc:m"
msgid ""
"Before <the_cataclysm> I worked in a lab.  Don't look at me like that, it "
"had nothing to do with this stuff… I was studying protein-protein "
"interactions in smooth muscle in mice, using NMR.  Nothing even vaguely "
"related to zombies.  Anyway, I was at last year's Experimental Biology "
"conference in San Francisco, and an old friend of mine was talking about "
"some really weird shit she'd heard of coming out of government labs.  Really "
"hush hush stuff.  Normally I wouldn't put much cred into that sort of thing, "
"but from her, it actually had me worried.  I packed a bug-out bag just in "
"case."
msgstr ""
"Antes del <the_cataclysm> que trabajara en un laboratorio. No me mires así, "
"no tenía nada que ver con esto... Estaba estudiando las interacciones "
"proteína-proteína en el músculo liso de los ratones, usando RMN. Nada que "
"esté vagamente relacionado con los zombis. De todos modos, estaba en la "
"conferencia de Biología Experimental del año pasado en San Francisco, y una "
"vieja amiga mía estaba hablando de una mierda muy rara que había oído de los "
"laboratorios del gobierno. Cosas realmente silenciosas. Normalmente no le "
"daría mucha credibilidad a ese tipo de cosas, pero de ella, me preocupaba. "
"Empaqué una mochila de escape por si acaso."

