msgid "Who are you?"
msgstr "¿Quién eres?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_MARLOSS_VOICE.json
msgid "Yes, friend?"
msgstr "¿Sí, amigo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_MARLOSS_VOICE.json
msgid "Yes… yes I have."
msgstr "Sí... sí tengo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_MARLOSS_VOICE.json
msgid "Your travels be fruitful, friend."
msgstr "Que tus viajes sean fructíferos, amigo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_MARLOSS_VOICE.json
msgid "[Take Marloss berry.] Thank you."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_NC_FARMER.json
msgid "A daring trader?  Yes.  Let's trade items."
msgstr "¿Un comerciante atrevido? Sí. Intercambiemos artículos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_NC_FARMER.json
msgid "Are you all right?"
msgstr "¿Estás bien?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_NC_FARMER.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "Are you one of them?"
msgstr "¿Eres uno de ellos?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_NC_FARMER.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "Are you one of them?"
msgstr "¿Eres uno de ellos?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_NC_FARMER.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "Are you one of them?"
msgstr "¿Eres uno de ellos?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_NC_FARMER.json
msgid ""
"Come a little closer, I don't want to make too much noise.  You smell much "
"nicer than what I'm used to.  Someone in trouble banged on the door that "
"night, she said she was desperate, she had a baby, her home had burned down "
"and her drugs were gone and there were monsters in the streets.  We figured "
"she was on drugs, but we couldn't turn them away so we gave them food and "
"let them stay in the barn."
msgstr ""
"Acércate un poco más, no quiero hacer mucho ruido. Hueles mucho mejor de lo "
"que estoy acostumbrado. Alguien con problemas llamó a la puerta esa noche, "
"dijo que estaba desesperada, que tenía un bebé, que su casa se había quemado "
"y que sus medicinas habían desaparecido y que había monstruos en las calles. "
"Supusimos que estaba drogada, pero no podíamos rechazarla, así que le dimos "
"comida y la dejamos quedarse en el granero."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_NC_FARMER.json
msgid "Have anything to trade?"
msgstr "¿Tienes algo para intercambiar?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
