"provide food, so I know you're thriving more than we are here.  All right, "
"I'll tell you what.  I'm not going anywhere without my friends here, we've "
"been through way too much together.  If you can convince Luo, Brandon, and "
"Yusuke to come along, then I'll go."
msgstr ""
"Bueno... habéis demostrado que puedes sobrevivir ahí fuera, y has sido capaz "
"de proporcionar comida, así que sé que estas prosperando más que nosotros "
"aquí. Mira, te voy a decir una cosa. No voy a ir a ninguna parte sin mis "
"amigos aquí, hemos pasado demasiadas cosas juntos. Si puedes convencer a "
"Luo, Brandon y Yusuke para que vengan, entonces los acompañaré."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid ""
"Well… you have shown that you can survive out there, and you've been able to "
"provide food, so I know you're thriving more than we are here.  All right, "
"I'll tell you what.  I'm not going anywhere without my friends here, we've "
"been through way too much together.  If you can convince Luo, Brandon, and "
"Yusuke to come along, then I'll go."
msgstr ""
"Bueno... habéis demostrado que puedes sobrevivir ahí fuera, y has sido capaz "
"de proporcionar comida, así que sé que estas prosperando más que nosotros "
"aquí. Mira, te voy a decir una cosa. No voy a ir a ninguna parte sin mis "
"amigos aquí, hemos pasado demasiadas cosas juntos. Si puedes convencer a "
"Luo, Brandon y Yusuke para que vengan, entonces los acompañaré."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"Where else?  I can't fight those things out there.  I'm in terrible physical "
"condition, don't have any useful skills, and I'm terrified of <zombies> and "
"violence.  How am I supposed to find a safe place?"
msgstr ""
"¿Dónde? No puedo luchar esas cosas de ahí fuera. Estoy en una condición "
"física terrible, no tengo ninguna habilidad útil, y estoy aterrorizado de "
"los <zombies> y la violencia. ¿Cómo se supone que voy a encontrar un lugar "
"seguro?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Why don't you scavenge your own food?"
msgstr "¿Por qué no rebuscar tu propia comida?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "About that shopping list of yours…"
msgstr "Sobre esa lista de compras tuya..."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
msgid "Actually can I ask you something else?"
msgstr "Espera, ¿te puedo preguntar otra cosa?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Any luck?  Bigger ones?"
msgstr "¿Ha habido suerte? ¿Las más grandes?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Are you seriously wearing a dinosaur costume?"
msgstr "¿En serio llevas puesto un disfraz de dinosaurio?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Brilliant!  You're a true hero.  I'll see if I can find a place to set these "
"up now."
msgstr ""
"¡Brillante! Eres un verdadero héroe. Veré si puedo encontrar un lugar para "
"colocar esto ahora."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
msgstr "Traer 10 cajas de cartón."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
msgstr "Trae 10 hojas de plástico grandes"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
msgstr "Traer 40 cajas pequeñas de cartón."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
msgstr "Trae 5 cajas de cartón grandes"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Cardboard?"
msgstr "¿Cartón?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Did you ask the masters?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Did you bring me those last few boxes?"
msgstr "¿Me trajiste las últimas cajas?"

#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Schizophrenic beggar in the refugee center.
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Dino Dave"
msgstr "Dino Dave"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Do you need something to eat?"
msgstr "¿Necesitas algo para comer?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Got the little ones yet?"
msgstr "¿Ya tienes a los pequeños?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Gotta start small right?  Little ones for keeping little things safe.  I "
"could use 'em."
msgstr ""
"Hay que empezar con algo pequeño, ¿no? Pequeños para mantener las cosas "
"pequeñas a salvo. Podría usarlos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Gotta start small right?  Little ones for keeping little things safe.  I "
"could use 'em.  I need a bunch of 'em.  Little ones, you know?  Can you "
"bring me like… like… forty?"
msgstr ""
"Hay que empezar con algo pequeño, ¿no? Pequeños para mantener las cosas "
"pequeñas a salvo. Podría usarlos. Necesito un puñado de ellos. Pequeños, "
"¿sabes? ¿Puedes traerme como... como... cuarenta?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Have I told you about cardboard, friend?  Do you have any?"
msgstr "¿Te he hablado sobre el cartón, amigo? ¿Tienes algo de cartón?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"How's things with you?  My cardboard collection is getting quite impressive."
msgstr ""
"¿Cómo están las cosas contigo? Mi colección de cartones se está volviendo "
"bastante impresionante."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"I can tell when it has stuff in it, it's got a sandy texture.  But this "
"doesn't.  Thanks again."
msgstr ""
"Puedo decirte cuando tiene algo dentro, tiene una textura arenosa. Pero esto "
"no. Gracias de nuevo."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I didn't think so."
msgstr "No lo creía."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I don't understand."
msgstr "No lo comprendo."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"I have it, I have it all, but I can't find a place to put it.  Will you ask "
"the masters?  Maybe?  I've tried but they ignore me."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"I have it, I have it all, but I can't find a place to put it.  Will you ask "
"the masters?  Maybe?  I've tried but they ignore me.  I just need a place to "
"put it all, a place I can be safe, and not make anyone upset."
msgstr ""
"Lo tengo, lo tengo todo pero no puedo encontrar un lugar para ponerlo. ¿Le "
"podrías preguntar a los maestros? ¿Tal vez? Lo intenté pero me ignoran. "
"Solamente necesito un lugar para poner todo, un lugar para estar seguro y no "
"molestar a nadie"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"I really feel bad sending you on this one, it's dangerous.  Have you found "
"anything?"
msgstr ""
"Me siento muy mal por enviarte a esta, es peligroso. ¿Has encontrado algo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I think I have to get going…"
msgstr "Tengo que irme ..."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I'll have to think on it, Dave, I've done a lot already."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I'll have to think on that, Dave, I've done a lot already."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I'll see you on the rooftop.  Good luck, Dave."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"I'm building a house out of cardboard.  The sandman doesn't want me to, but "
"I told him to go fuck himself."
msgstr ""
"Estoy construyendo una casa de cartón. El hombre de arena no quiere que lo "
"haga, pero le dije que se fuera a la mierda."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I'm so happy now!"
msgstr "¡Estoy tan feliz ahora!"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"If I can set it up in here I won't need it, but they might drive me out, so "
"I guess I need some plastic just in case.  I don't like it, the sandman can "
"smell through plastic, but I think the cardboard is stronger."
msgstr ""
"Si puedo instalarlo aquí no lo necesitaré, pero podrían echarme, así que "
"supongo que necesito algo de plástico por si acaso. No me gusta, el hombre "
"de arena puede oler a través del plástico, pero creo que el cartón es más "
"fuerte."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"If I can set it up in here I won't need it, but they might drive me out, so "
"I guess I need some plastic just in case.  I don't like it, the sandman can "
"smell through plastic, but I think the cardboard is stronger.  Please bring "
"me some plastic sheets."
msgstr ""
"Si puedo instalarlo aquí no lo necesitaré, pero podrían echarme, así que "
"supongo que necesito algo de plástico por si acaso. No me gusta, el hombre "
"de arena puede oler a través del plástico, pero creo que el cartón es más "
"fuerte. Por favor, tráeme unas láminas de plástico."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"If you don't know who he is, I definitely can't tell you.  He talks to "
"everyone, if you didn't hear him that means you can't be trusted, except to "
"help me out."
msgstr ""
"Si no sabes quién es, definitivamente no puedo decírtelo. Habla con todo el "
"mundo, si no lo escuchaste significa que no se puede confiar en ti, excepto "
"para ayudarme."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Is there anything else I can do for you?"
msgstr "¿Hay algo más que pueda hacer por ti?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "It's all around us… but did you get it in a crude matter form?"
msgstr ""
"Está a nuestro alrededor... ¿pero lo conseguiste en forma de materia prima?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I… I can see you wearing it.  Why are you wearing that?"
msgstr "Yo... puedo ver que lo llevas puesto. ¿Por qué llevas eso?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Kind of a question's that?  Yeah man, you got cardboard, I got a whole… a "
"whole shopping list.  Got it here."
msgstr ""
"¿Que clase de pregunta es esa? Sí, tío, tú tienes cartón, yo tengo toda... "
"toda una lista de la compra. La tengo aquí."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Maybe somewhere they can't see me?  Where I can just be me?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Nice, this will do perfectly!"
msgstr "¡Bien, esto servirá perfectamente!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"No!  I just got everything together.  I am not leaving, not now.  "
"Everything's finally coming together!"
msgstr ""
"¡No! Acabo de reunilor todo. No me voy a ir, no ahora. ¡Todo se está "
"resolviendo por fin!"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "No!  Oh god, no, this can't be happening…"
msgstr "No! Oh Dios, no, esto no puede estar ocurriendo..."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "No, I don't."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "No."
msgstr "No."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Nobody's the same, not even twins.  But I'll tell you something.  The big "
"eye looked at me.  When it did, it heard the voices, and it blinked."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Oh man, but we're so close!"
msgstr "¡Oh hombre, pero estamos tan cerca!"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Oh man, thanks so much my friend.  You won't regret it."
msgstr "Oh hombre, muchas gracias amigo. No te arrepentirás."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Oh this is so great, so great!"
msgstr "¡Oh, esto es demasido grande, mejor aún!"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Oh, that's too bad."
msgstr "Qué lástima."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Oh, that's too bad.  Guess they're eating it all."
msgstr "Oh, qué pena. Supongo que se los están comiendo todo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Once I saw the full moon, and it was staring right at me - only it couldn't "
"see me, because the sandman kept it away.  Understand?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Shields?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Sure, Dave.  One last favor, I think I can talk to Smokes about finding you "
"a place to go."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to call home."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Ten bigger ones now please.  The list doesn't lie.  You've done so well."
msgstr ""
"Diez más grandes ahora, por favor. La lista no miente. Lo has hecho tan bien."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Ten bigger ones now please.  The list doesn't lie.  You've done so well.  I "
"got a little more on the list, but we're more than half there."
msgstr ""
"Diez más grandes ahora, por favor. La lista no miente. Lo has hecho tan "
"bien. Tengo un poco más en la lista, pero ya estamos a más de la mitad."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Thank you!  I'm sorry, I thought we were done, but we can do this!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "That's OK, nobody's perfect, ha ha…"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"The roof!  So high!  So lofty!  Come see me there, my friend.  I will not "
"disappoint you."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"The roof!  So high!  So lofty!  I can hardly believe it!  This will be a "
"nicer house than I had before everything went funny.  I can watch out, I'm "
"happy to do that.  And it'll be nice to still have a bathroom!  Come see me "
"there, my friend.  I will not disappoint you."
msgstr ""
"¡El techo! ¡Tan alto! ¡Tan elevado! ¡Me cuesta asimilarlo! Esta va a ser una "
"casa mejor que la que tenía antes de que todo se pusiera raro. Puedo estar "
"atento a los zombis, con gusto lo haré. ¡Y va a estar bueno tener un baño! "
"Ven a hablar conmigo, amigo. No te voy a decepcionar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "The sandman?"
msgstr "¿El hombre de arena?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"There's so much of it now, and the zombies are afraid of it.  It's kept me "
"safe so far.  The beta rays come from the center point of the zombie, so it "
"hits the cardboard and can't penetrate.  The reflection can stop any further "
"damage."
msgstr ""
"Porque ahora hay mucho y los zombis le tienen miedo. Me mantiene a salvo. "
"Los rayos beta vienen del punto central del zombi, así que golpea el cartón "
"y no lo puede penetrar. La reflexión puede frenar los daños."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"These cowards are afraid of me.  They won't let me into their base.  I'm "
"going to build my new house and I won't let them in."
msgstr ""
"Estos cobardes me tienen miedo. No me dejan entrar en su base. Voy a "
"construir mi nueva casa y no los dejaré entrar."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"These ones are good, good ones.  They need something to, you know, bind them "
"together.  Surround them, light side, dark side."
msgstr ""
"Estos son buenos, de los buenos. Necesitan algo para, ya sabes, juntarlos. "
"Rodéalos, lado luminoso, lado oscuro,"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"These ones are good, good ones.  They need something to, you know, bind them "
"together.  Surround them, light side, dark side.  Bring me the Force!"
msgstr ""
"Estos son buenos, de los buenos. Necesitan algo para, ya sabes, juntarlos. "
"Rodéalos, lado luminoso, lado oscuro. ¡Tráeme la Fuerza!"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "They keep a lot of this stuff in hardware stores and lumber yards."
msgstr "Guardan un montón de estas cosas en ferreterías y madereras."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"This is the last thing I need from you.  I've been collecting the other "
"parts myself, it's been easier with more cardboard around.  Can you bring me "
"five more really big cardboard boxes?"
msgstr ""
"Esto es lo último que necesito de ti. He estado coleccionando las otras "
"partes yo mismo, habría sido más fácil con más cartón alrededor. ¿Puedes "
"traerme cinco cajas de cartón realmente grandes?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"This is the last thing I need from you.  I've been collecting the other "
"parts myself, it's been easier with more cardboard around.  Can you bring me "
"five more really big cardboard boxes?  Five more cardboard boxes, as big as "
"it gets.  I have a few already stored up, that should be all I need."
msgstr ""
"Esto es lo último que necesito de ti. He estado coleccionando las otras "
"partes yo mismo, ha sido más fácil con más cartón alrededor. ¿Puedes traerme "
"cinco cajas de cartón realmente grandes? Cinco cajas de cartón más, tan "
"grandes como sea posible. Ya tengo unas cuantas almacenadas, eso debería ser "
"todo lo que necesito."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Try looking in cargo storage areas."
msgstr "Intenta buscar en las zonas de almacenamiento de carga."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Watch out, he's looking for it too."
msgstr "Cuidado, él también lo está buscando."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "We're almost there, now."
msgstr "Ya casi llegamos, ahora."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "We've done it!  We've solved the list!"
msgstr "¡Lo hemos conseguido! ¡Hemos terminado la lista!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"We've done it, Dave!  Smokes says you can build yourself a house up on the "
"roof if you want.  You've got to keep it nice and clean, and help out the "
"people down here by looking out for zombies, but you can still use the "
"washrooms and things downstairs when you need to.  What do you say?"
msgstr ""
"¡Lo hicimos, Dave! Humos dice que puedes construirte una casa en el tejado "
"si quieres. Tienes que mantenerla bonita y limpia, y ayudar a la gente de "
"aquí abajo vigilando que no haya zombis, pero puedes seguir usando los "
"lavabos y las cosas de abajo cuando lo necesites. ¿Qué te parece?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Well, OK then, Dave.  One last favor, I think I can talk to Smokes about "
"finding you a place to go."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Well… I had it all pretty together, "
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "What are you going to do with all that cardboard now?"
msgstr "¿Qué vas a hacer con todo ese cartón ahora?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "What was that about cardboard?"
msgstr "¿Qué es eso del cartón?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "What's next on the list?"
msgstr "¿Qué es lo siguiente en la lista?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Why are you sitting out here?"
msgstr "¿Por qué estás sentado aquí?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Why cardboard?"
msgstr "¿Y por qué de cartón?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Why don't you leave this place?  Come with me, I could use some help out "
"there."
msgstr ""
"¿Por qué no dejas este lugar? Ven conmigo, me vendría bien algo de ayuda ahí "
"fuera."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Would you like me to give you some cardboard?"
msgstr "¿Quieres que te dé algo de cartón?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid ""
"Yeah, I'm real hungry and they put drugs in most of the food.  I can see "
"you're not like that."
msgstr ""
"Sí, tengo mucha hambre y le ponen drogas a la mayoría de la comida. Puedo "
"ver que no eres así."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid ""
"Yeah, I'm real hungry and they put drugs in most of the food.  I can see "
"you're not like that."
msgstr ""
"Sí, tengo mucha hambre y le ponen drogas a la mayoría de la comida. Puedo "
"ver que no eres así."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid ""
"Yeah, I'm real hungry and they put drugs in most of the food.  I can see "
"you're not like that."
msgstr ""
"Sí, tengo mucha hambre y le ponen drogas a la mayoría de la comida. Puedo "
"ver que no eres así."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Yes!  The home stretch!"
msgstr "¡Sí! ¡La recta final!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"You ask me what I can see, but I don't tell you what you see.  Sometimes we "
"have shields up, to protect ourselves."
msgstr ""
"Me preguntas lo que puedo ver, pero no te digo lo que tu ves. A veces "
"tenemos los escudos levantados para protegernos de nosotros mismos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "You said you were building a house?"
msgstr "¿Dijiste que estabas construyendo una casa?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "[Schizophrenic] I think I do.  Are we the same?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "and I feel bad with all the help you've given me already, but "
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"now the masters won't let me build my sanctuary.  I know I can't build it in "
"here, they wouldn't allow it.  They won't listen to me when I ask for a safe "
"place.  They just want me to disappear, like the others.  Can you help me "
"figure them out?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "…What were you saying before?"
msgstr "...¿Qué decías antes?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid ""
"Actually yeah, I'm always hungry these days.  I don't like taking handouts, "
"but I wouldn't say no."
msgstr ""
"En realidad sí, siempre tengo hambre estos días. No me gustan las limosnas "
"pero no te lo voy a rechazar."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid ""
"Aw damn, I was worried you'd say that.  Okay, listen: you've got yourself a "
"deal.  I'll come to your base, but you've gotta get me hooked up with a "
"microscope as soon as you can.  This could be the beginning of something "
"really cool.  Oh, and it should go without saying that I'm not coming unless "
"you can find a place for my friends here in your base.  I'm sure you "
"anticipated that.  Talk them into going and I'm in.  It should be easy, "
"they're a bunch of sweet hearted saps."
msgstr ""
"Maldición, me preocupaba que dijeras eso. Bien, escucha: tienes un trato. "
"Iré a tu base, pero tienes que conectarme con un microscopio tan pronto como "
"puedas. Esto podría ser el comienzo de algo realmente genial. Y no hace "
"falta decir que no iré a menos que encuentres un lugar para mis amigos aquí "
"en tu base. Estoy seguro de que te has anticipado a eso. Habla con ellos "
"para que vayan y yo me apunto. Debería ser fácil, son un montón de tontos de "
"corazón dulce."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Do you know about the fungal zombies though?"
msgstr "¿Sabes lo de los zombis fúngicos?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid ""
"Does that mean you were part of that back room evacuation I heard about?"
msgstr ""
"¿Eso significa que fuiste parte de la evacuación del cuarto trasero de la "
"que me enteré?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Don't bother with these assholes."
msgstr "No te molestes con estos capullos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid ""
"Don't get me wrong, I hate this place and this situation, and especially the "
"selfish racist fucks that landed me here… but these other losers that landed "
"out here with me?  I like them.  We might be miserable, but we're miserable "
"together."
msgstr ""
"No me malinterpretes, odio este lugar y esta situación, y especialmente a "
"los egoistas racistas de mierda que me trajeron aquí... pero, ¿estos "
"perdedores que me trajeron aquí?. Me gustan. Puede que seamos miserables, "
"pero lo seremos juntos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid ""
"Encroaching alien mushrooms, fungal towers, tough mycelium invading ground "
"and trees, zombies taken over by aggressive mold… Yeah.  It's ugly stuff."
msgstr ""
"Hongos alienígenas invasores, torres fúngicas, micelios resistentes que "
"invaden el suelo y los árboles, zombis invadidos por un agresivo moho... Sí. "
"Es algo feo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid ""
"Even without them helping, it's the safest place to squat.  As long as we "
"keep it clean up here and don't cause sanitation problems, they don't mind "
"us sitting around the entryway.  So kind and generous of them, to let us sit "
"here and slowly starve."
msgstr ""
"Incluso sin su ayuda, es el lugar más seguro para quedarse. Mientras "
"mantengamos limpio  el sitio y no causemos problemas sanitarios, no les "
"importa que nos sentemos cerca de la entrada. Son tan amables y generosos "
"por dejar sentarnos aquí a morirnos de hambre."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid ""
"Glad you like it.  If I think of something you can do in return, I'll let "
"you know."
msgstr ""
"Me alegro de que te guste. Si se me ocurre algo que puedas hacer a cambio, "
"te lo haré saber."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Great!  I'll go see what I can do about that."
msgstr "¡Genial! Iré a ver qué puedo hacer al respecto."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid ""
"Heh.  Yeah, that was a great use of my time.  As you can see it really "
"helped my employment prospects.  Yeah, I have a PhD in mycology.  Did my "
"dissertation on signaling pathways in hyphae formation, and a postdoc in "
"plant-fungus communication in rhizomes.  Then I got the job at the bookstore "
"because there wasn't a ton of work for a doctor of mycology, although I'd "
"had a few nibbles before things really got crazy.  Now, people are just "
"breaking down my door to get my sweet sweet knowledge of mold to help them "
"fight the incoming zombie threat."
msgstr ""
"Heh. Sí, eso fue un gran uso de mi tiempo. Como puedes ver, realmente ayudó "
"a mis perspectivas de empleo. Sí, tengo un doctorado en micología. Hice mi "
"disertación sobre las vías de señalización en la formación de hifas, y un "
"postdoctorado en comunicación planta-hongo en rizomas. Luego conseguí el "
"trabajo en la librería porque no había mucho trabajo para un doctor en "
"micología, aunque había comido algunos bocados antes de que las cosas se "
"volvieran realmente locas. Ahora, la gente está derribando mi puerta para "
"obtener mi dulce conocimiento del moho para ayudarles a luchar contra la "
"amenaza zombi inminente."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "I don't care if you're Chinese.  You can travel with me if you want."
msgstr "No me importa si eres chino. Puedes viajar conmigo si quieres."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid ""
"I dunno, scientific interest?  If you don't bring me anything, no worries.  "
"I'm positively swimming in entertainment here, as you can see."
msgstr ""
"No sé, ¿interés científico? Si no me traes nada, no te preocupes. Estoy "
"nadando positivamente en el entretenimiento aquí, como puedes ver."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "I found a sample of alien fungus for you."
msgstr "Encontré una muestra de hongo alienígena para ti."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid ""
"I have a camp of my own, away from here.  No paperwork required.  Want to "
"come?"
msgstr ""
"Tengo mi propio campamento, lejos de aquí. No se requiere ningún papeleo. "
"¿Quieres venir?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid ""
"I mean, racism could definitely be a part of it… but you are visibly in poor "
"shape.  They need strong survivor material."
msgstr ""
"Quiero decir, el racismo podría ser parte de ello... pero tú estás "
"visiblemente en mala forma. Necesitan material de supervivencia fuerte."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "I might have some food for you.  Are you hungry?"
msgstr "Puede que tenga algo de comida para ti. ¿Tienes hambre?"

#. ~ Name of effect type id "insulted_luo"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Insulted"
msgstr "Insultado"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "It just so happens I have a chunk of fungal matter on me right now."
msgstr "Sucede que tengo un trozo de materia fúngica sobre mí ahora mismo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid ""
"It may not be much, but we've got a little community.  We can't live like "
"this forever, but we're safer than out there, and we look out for each "
"other.  One way or another we'll shake things out to something better."
msgstr ""
"Puede que no sea mucho, pero tenemos una pequeña comunidad. No podemos vivir "
"así para siempre, pero estamos más seguros que allá afuera, y nos cuidamos "
"los unos a los otros. De una forma u otra cambiaremos las cosas por algo "
"mejor."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid ""
"It'd be dangerous.  What kind of benefit is there from taking a risk like "
"that?"
msgstr ""
"Sería peligroso. ¿Qué clase de beneficio hay en tomar un riesgo como ese?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid ""
"It'd be temporary.  I have a base set up.  There are only a few of us "
"survivors left, we need to work together"
msgstr ""
"Sería temporal. Tengo una base instalada. Sólo quedamos unos pocos "
"supervivientes, tenemos que trabajar juntos..."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Just wanted to get square.  I'd better get going."
msgstr "Sólo quería ser honesto. Será mejor que me vaya."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid ""
"Like I said, sorry, it's just not happening.  It's not that I don't trust "
"you, it's just that I don't really trust you."
msgstr ""
"Como dije, lo siento, no está sucediendo. No es que no confíe en ti, es sólo "
"que no confío en ti."

#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
#. ~ Angry beggar in the refugee center.
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Luo Meizhen"
msgstr "Luo Meizhen"

#. ~ Name suffix of a female NPC
#. ~ Angry beggar in the refugee center.
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Mycologist"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "No problem.  See you."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid ""
"No, no I don't, and I'd appreciate you not leaving me hanging on that.  "
"There are fungal zombies?"
msgstr ""
"No, no lo hago, y te agradecería que no me dejaras pendiente de eso. ¿Hay "
"zombis de hongos?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid ""
"Oh yeah, that was a hell of a shitstorm.  We were waiting back there for "
"'processing' for hours and hours, with the sick and wounded.  One guy died, "
"we all thought he was sleeping until he got back up.  That started a panic, "
"gunshots in a closed area, that kind of stuff.  In just a few minutes, a "
"bunch more people were dead.  Then the assholes called it an 'outbreak' and "
"tried to barricade us in… took us way too long to convince the panicking "
"guards that we were alive and needed to get out.  I'll give the one guy "
"credit, Sean: when he found out they'd locked living people in with zombies, "
"he came in himself, as some of the newly dead were starting to get back up, "
"and he held them off for us to escape.  That… that was probably the only "
"actual good thing I've seen since before the end of the world: he owned his "
"error and he put himself in harm's way to make up for it.  Massive respect "
"to that guy.  So, of course, he's a zombie now.  Fuck, thanks for reminding "
"me of all that sunny fun."
msgstr ""
"Oh sí, eso fue una gran tormenta de mierda. Estuvimos esperando allí atrás "
"para \"procesar\" durante horas y horas, con los enfermos y heridos. Un tipo "
"murió, todos pensamos que estaba durmiendo hasta que se levantó. Eso inició "
"el pánico, disparos en un área cerrada, ese tipo de cosas. En sólo unos "
"minutos, un montón de gente más estaba muerta. Entonces los imbéciles lo "
"llamaron un \"brote\" y trataron de atrincherarnos dentro... ...nos tomó "
"demasiado tiempo convencer a los guardias en pánico de que estábamos vivos y "
"que necesitábamos salir. Le daré crédito a un tipo, Sean: cuando descubrió "
"que habían encerrado a gente viva con zombis, entró él mismo, ya que algunos "
"de los recién muertos estaban empezando a levantarse, y los retuvo para que "
"escapáramos. Eso... eso fue probablemente la única cosa buena que he visto "
"desde antes del fin del mundo: se adueñó de su error y se puso en peligro "
"para compensarlo. Un respeto enorme a ese tipo. Así que, por supuesto, ahora "
"es un zombi. Joder, gracias por recordarme toda esa diversión soleada."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid ""
"Oh, come on.  I'm not a random stranger anymore, I brought you that crazy "
"mushroom didn't I?"
msgstr "Oh, vamos. Ya no soy un extraño al azar, te traje esa seta loca, ¿no?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid ""
"Oh, same old story at first.  I got evacuated on to the local concentration "
"center, then picked up on a repurposed school bus and dragged out here.  "
"Then the chick processing me to get in saw my face and Chinese name and "
"conveniently 'lost' my paperwork.  I was sent out here to wait for further "
"processing, while I watched busloads of people get processed and taken in.  "
"By the time they 'found' it, the place was full up, wouldn't ya know it.  "
"Now I'm stuck out here and they won't consider letting me in."
msgstr ""
"Oh, misma historia de siempre al principio. Me evacuaron al centro de "
"concentración local, luego me recogieron en un autobús escolar reutilizado y "
"me trajeron aquí. Luego, la chica encargada de procesarme para entrar vio mi "
"cara y mi nombre chino y convenientemente \"perdió\" mi documentación. Me "
"enviaron aquí para esperar más procesamiento, mientras veía cómo se "
"procesaba y se llevaban a montones de personas. Para cuando lo "
"\"encontraron\", el lugar estaba lleno, ¿quién lo hubiera dicho? Ahora estoy "
"atrapado aquí y no considerarán dejarme entrar."

#. ~ Description of effect type "Insulted"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Oh, you went there."
msgstr "Oh, tú fuiste allí."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Okay, yeah, that's a bit of a problem.  What were you saying before?"
msgstr "Vale, sí, eso es un pequeño problema. ¿Qué decías antes?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid ""
"Okay, you've got my attention.  Listen, do you think you could bring me some "
"kind of sample of these things?"
msgstr ""
"Bien, tienes mi atención. Escucha, ¿crees que podrías traerme algún tipo de "
"muestra de estas cosas?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Ok… see ya."
msgstr "Ok... nos vemos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid ""
"Oooooh.  Oh.  You did not just fucking go there.  Let's leave the fatties to "
"die, hey?  Wanna know how easy it is to find fucking *thyroid medication* "
"after the apocalypse, asshat?  Besides, there are more skills than heavy "
"lifting needed now… no, you know what?  Screw it.  You're not worth my time."
msgstr ""
"Oooooh. Oh. No acabas de ir allí. Dejemos que los gordos mueran, ¿eh? "
"¿Quieres saber lo fácil que es encontrar la maldita *medicación para la "
"tiroides* después del apocalipsis, imbécil? Además, hay más habilidades que "
"el levantamiento de pesas que se necesitan ahora... no, ¿sabes qué? Que te "
"den. No mereces mi tiempo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
