"what I can.  I must ask a small amount in trade, for materials.  I hope you "
"understand."
msgstr ""
"Sí, mi amigo. Has hecho mucho por mí, estaría encantado de enseñarte lo que "
"pueda. Debo pedir una pequeña cantidad a cambio, por los materiales. Espero "
"que lo entiendas."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find someone to clean up the back bay."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid ""
"Yes, please.  If you can ask around for someone who can help, I can gather "
"the tools they will need and some payment for them."
msgstr ""
"Sí, por favor. Si puedes preguntar por ahí por alguien que pueda ayudar, "
"puedo reunir las herramientas que necesitarás y algún pago por ellas."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find someone to clean up the back bay."
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris a circular saw."
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris his son's lost writing."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid "You are a kind soul."
msgstr "Eres un alma bondadosa."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris his son's lost writing."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid "You can tell it is his because he covered it in stickers."
msgstr "Se puede decir que es suyo porque lo ha revistió de pegatinas."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid "You don't seem to be doing great."
msgstr "No parece que te vaya bien."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid "[Leave Boris alone for now.]"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid ""
"…Ash.  His name was Ash, and he was ten years old.  Such a light, a spark.  "
"I wanted to see the man he would grow into.  I… now I can barely say his "
"name.  I miss him so much, every instant.  If I did not have Stan, I would "
"walk out through the barbed wire and join the walking dead."
msgstr ""
"...Ash. Su nombre era Ash, y tenía diez años. Una luz, una chispa. Quería "
"ver el hombre en el que se convertiría. Yo... ahora apenas puedo decir su "
"nombre. Lo extraño tanto, a cada segundo. Si no tuviera a Stan, saldría por "
"el alambre de púas y me uniría a los muertos vivientes."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "*beams at you as you approach.  \""
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"*is a pale woman with a broad, friendly face.  She seems to start opening "
"with a wide grin, then notices her somber surroundings and dials it back to "
"a pleasant smile.  \"Hi there.  I'm Dana, Dana Nunez.  Nice to see a new "
"face.\""
msgstr ""
"*es una mujer pálida con una cara amigable y ancha. Parece empezar con una "
"sonrisa amplia pero se da cuenta de sus alrededores sombríos y disminuye a "
"una sonrisa simpática. \"Hola. Soy Dana, Dana Nuñez. Es bueno ver a alguien "
"nuevo.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"*takes the jar from you eagerly, studying it with care.  \"He's been through "
"a lot, hasn't he.  Poor guy.  Aw man.\"  She turns back to you, beaming.  "
"\"Oh, you will not regret this.  He may not look like much, but he's got it "
"where it counts, kid.  It's gonna take me a few days to revive him after "
"being abandoned so long, but he'll be operational soon and then you can come "
"back for some real bread.\"  She frowns.  \"I don't really have much to give "
"you in return, but I'll cut you a deal on bread if that helps.\""
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"*turns from her conversation with Pablo, and smiles as she sees you.  \""
msgstr "*abandona su conversación con Pablo y sonríe cuando te ve. \""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"All right, old buddy.  You know, I know what he means to you.  I'll take "
"good care of him, so that he won't get a scratch."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"All right.  I've taken some time to think about it, and I'm willing to go.  "
"I'm sure they'll have use for a baker over there, after all, and if I don't "
"get out of this place there's a very real chance I'm going to snap.  You can "
"go let Pablo know first hand, if you want; he's been pretty excited about "
"the idea."
msgstr ""
"Está bien. Me he tomado un tiempo para pensarlo y estoy dispuesto a ir. "
"Estoy seguro de que les servirá un panadero de allí, después de todo, y si "
"no salgo de este lugar hay una posibilidad muy real de que me desmorone. "
"Puedes ir a decírselo a Pablo de primera mano, si quieres; haestá muy "
"entusiasmado con la idea."

#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "Dana Nunez"
msgstr "Dana Nunez"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "Dana's family sourdough starter"
msgid_plural "Dana's family sourdough starter"
msgstr[0] "iniciador de masa madre de la familia de Dana"
msgstr[1] "iniciadores de masa madre de la familia de Dana"
msgstr[2] "iniciadores de masa madre de la familia de Dana"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "Dana's sourdough bread"
msgid_plural "Dana's sourdough bread"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "Dana, hey?  Nice to meet you.  How are things here?"
msgstr "¿Dana? Encantada de conocerte. ¿Cómo van las cosas por aquí?"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "Find Dana's family sourdough culture"
msgstr "Encuentra la Cultura de la Masa Madre de la familia de Dana"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "Got any more bread I can trade flour for?"
msgstr "¿Tienes más pan por el que intercambiar por harina?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"Great, here's a loaf of my locally-famous, not-very-mature sourdough.  It's "
"not too bad honestly.  Everyone here seems to like it."
msgstr ""
"Genial, aquí hay una barra de mi localmente famoso, no muy maduro pan "
"fermentado. No está tan mal, honestamente. A todos aquí parece gustarles."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "Have you done any baking lately?"
msgstr "¿Has horneado algo últimamente?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Dana's family sourdough culture"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"He'll be in the right-hand fridge, in a jar with a picture of the Millennium "
"Falcon on it."
msgstr ""
"Estará en la nevera de la derecha, en un frasco con una foto del Halcón "
"Milenario."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "Hello, nice to see you again.  What brings you around today?"
msgstr "Hola, me alegro de verte de nuevo. ¿Qué te trae por aquí hoy?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "Hi Dana, nice to meet you.  I gotta go though."
msgstr "Hola Dana, encantado de conocerte. Tengo que irme."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "Hi Dana, nice to see you too.  I gotta go though."
msgstr "Hola Dana, yo también me alegro de verte. Tengo que irme."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"Huh.  I've made a few friends here, but not so much as I'd stick around here "
"with no future prospects, hoping someone downstairs dies to make room for "
"me.  It does sound nice, if they're looking for more workers."
msgstr ""
"Huh. He hecho algunos amigos aquí, pero no tanto como para quedarme aquí sin "
"perspectivas de futuro, esperando que alguien de abajo muera para hacerme "
"sitio. Suena bien, si estás buscando más trabajadores."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Dana's family sourdough culture"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"I am not sure if I'm gonna make it through the Cataclysm without my special "
"jar of goop."
msgstr ""
"No estoy seguro de si voy a pasar el Cataclismo sin mi tarro especial de "
"pringue."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Dana's family sourdough culture"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"I can understand why you think you wouldn't want to risk your life for a "
"bread starter.  You haven't tried that bread."
msgstr ""
"Puedo entender por qué crees que no querrías arriesgar tu vida por un "
"iniciador de pan. No has probado ese pan."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Dana's family sourdough culture"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "I could get my real sourdough starter…"
msgstr "Podría conseguir mi verdadera masa madre de entrante..."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"I do a bit.  I got a sourdough starter going almost as soon as I arrived, "
"and it's making passable bread already.  I cooked some up yesterday "
"actually, I could probably trade a loaf of fresh bread for, say, about eight "
"cups of flour, or two merch."
msgstr ""
"Lo hago un poco. Tengo un entrante de masa madre casi desde que llegué, y ya "
"está haciendo pan pasable. Ayer cociné un poco, probablemente podría cambiar "
"una barra de pan fresco por, digamos, ocho tazas de harina o dos merc."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "I guess I'm outta here then."
msgstr "Supongo que me voy de aquí entonces."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"I spoke to the foreman over at Tacoma Ranch.  If you're willing to put in "
"the work, they'll find some work for you over there."
msgstr ""
"Hablé con el capataz del Rancho Tacoma. Si estás dispuesto a trabajar, te "
"encontrarán un trabajo allí."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"I spoke to your husband about getting you a job at the Tacoma Ranch.  What "
"would you think about that?"
msgstr ""
"Hablé con su marido para que le consiguiera un trabajo en el Rancho Tacoma. "
"¿Qué pensarías de eso?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"I was working in a nice restaurant as a baker, until <the_cataclysm>.  I was "
"pregnant, and it was getting close to time to go on mat leave; lots of time "
"on my feet, getting up stupid-early to make pastries, you know.  Because of "
"the pregnancy we were evacuated early and shipped out this way, but our bus "
"was attacked in the chaos.  We managed to escape, but had to hike the rest "
"of the way, with the Singhs and a few other refugees that didn't make it.  I "
"lost the baby.  It wasn't a good time."
msgstr ""
"Yo estaba trabajando en un buen restaurante como panadero, hasta el "
"<the_cataclysm> Estaba embarazada, y se acercaba la hora de ir de permiso de "
"maternidad; mucho tiempo de pie, levantándome estúpidamente temprano para "
"hacer pasteles, ya sabes. Debido al embarazo fuimos evacuados temprano y "
"enviados por este camino, pero nuestro autobús fue atacado en el caos. "
"Logramos escapar, pero tuvimos que caminar el resto del camino, con los "
"Singhs y algunos otros refugiados que no lo lograron. Perdí al bebé. No fue "
"un buen momento."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "I'd better get going.  Bye, Dana."
msgstr "Será mejor que me vaya. Adiós, Dana."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "I'll hold you to that."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "I'll look into that.  I'd better get going though."
msgstr "Lo investigaré. Será mejor que me vaya."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "I'll look into that.  What were you saying before?"
msgstr "Lo investigaré. ¿Qué decías antes?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "I'm just glad to help."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "I've got your sourdough."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Dana's family sourdough culture"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"If you really like this second-rate bread, you could risk your life for "
"something actually worth it.  I left my actual sourdough starter back in the "
"bakery where I worked.  That baby is a hundred years old, and has been in my "
"family for generations… if you can bring him to me, I'll bake you the finest "
"bread you've ever had."
msgstr ""
"Si realmente te gusta este pan de segunda categoría, podrías arriesgar tu "
"vida por algo que realmente valga la pena. Deje mi arranque de pan de masa "
"madre en la panadería donde trabajaba. Si me lo traes, te haré el mejor pan "
"que hayas probado."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "It smells awesome.  I'm going to head out now, thanks!"
msgstr "Huele genial. Voy a salir ahora, ¡gracias!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
msgid "It's good to see you're still around."
msgstr "Es bueno ver que todavía estás por aquí."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "Maybe not right now, I think I'd better go."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "Nice to meet you, Dana.  What's your story?"
msgstr "Encantado de conocerte, Dana. ¿Cuál es tu historia?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"Oh, fine.  Six cups of flour, or one merch.  I'm not going any lower, I got "
"a business to run here."
msgstr ""
"Oh, bien. Seis tazas de harina, o un merc. No voy a bajar más, tengo un "
"negocio que llevar aquí."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Dana's family sourdough culture"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"Oh, you will not regret this.  He may not look like much, but he's got it "
"where it counts, kid.  It's gonna take me a few days to revive him after "
"being abandoned so long, but he'll be operational soon and then you can come "
"back for some real bread."
msgstr ""
"Oh, no te arrepentirás de esto. Puede que no parezca gran cosa, pero lo "
"tiene donde cuenta, chico. Me llevará unos días revivirlo después de estar "
"tanto tiempo abandonado, pero pronto estará operativo y entonces podrás "
"volver a por un poco de pan de verdad."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"Pablo's a little quicker on the trigger than I am.  We're trying to have a "
"baby, did you know that?  It's a bit crazy in this world, but I won't change "
"those plans.  Tell you what: if your camp has access to a doctor and some "
"medical facilities, in case I actually can get pregnant again, I would "
"consider getting out of here and signing up."
msgstr ""
"Pablo es un poco más rápido en el gatillo que yo. Estamos tratando de tener "
"un bebé, ¿lo sabías? Es un poco loco en este mundo, pero no cambiaré esos "
"planes. Te diré algo: si tu campamento tiene acceso a un doctor y a algunas "
"instalaciones médicas, en caso de que pueda quedar embarazada de nuevo, "
"consideraría salir de aquí y apuntarme."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "Right.  Sure."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Dana's family sourdough culture"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "So, you seen my sourdough starter?"
msgstr "Entonces, ¿has visto mi iniciador de masa madre?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"Sorry, it's not something I can bend on.  I don't make a big profit off "
"this, I use what I get to make more bread.  If I cut you a deal, I'll run "
"out of supplies."
msgstr ""
"Lo siento, no es algo que pueda doblar. No obtengo grandes beneficios de "
"esto, uso lo que obtengo para hacer más pan. Si te hago un buen trato, me "
"quedaré sin suministros."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"Sorry, not quite yet.  Landough was in pretty rough shape.  No fault of "
"yours, it was no good having him cooped up in a dank fridge for that long… "
"and I think my apprentice baker may have fucked with him before the "
"Cataclysm too.  He'd better hope he's a zombie now, because if I see him "
"alive… anyway, it's gonna take a few more feeds before I can get him ready "
"for prime time, check back in a couple days."
msgstr ""
"Lo siento, todavía no. Landough estaba en una forma bastante mala. No es "
"culpa tuya, no era bueno tenerlo encerrado en una nevera húmeda tanto "
"tiempo... y creo que mi aprendiz de panadero puede haberlo jodido antes del "
"Cataclismo también. Más vale que espere ser un zombi ahora, porque si lo veo "
"vivo... ...de todos modos, va a tomar unas cuantas sesiones más antes de que "
"pueda tenerlo listo para el horario de máxima audiencia, vuelve en un par de "
"días."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "Sure, I'll go tell him.  Cool!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"Sure.  If you really like this second-rate bread, you could risk your life "
"for something actually worth it.  I left my actual sourdough starter back in "
"the bakery where I worked.  That baby is a hundred years old, and has been "
"in my family for generations… if you can bring him to me, I'll bake you the "
"finest bread you've ever had."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Dana's family sourdough culture"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"Take care of yourself out there.  And listen, when you bring my sourdough "
"back, I don't want to see a scratch on him, you understand?"
msgstr ""
"Cuídate ahí fuera. Y escucha, cuando me devuelvas mi masa madre, no quiero "
"ver un rasguño en él, ¿entiendes?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"Take care of yourself out there.\"  She jots down directions to her bakery "
"and hands them to you.  \"His name is Landough, Landough Calrisean.  He'll "
"be in the right-hand fridge, in a jar with a picture of the Millennium "
"Falcon on it.  And listen, when you bring my sourdough back, I don't want to "
"see a scratch on him, you understand?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "Thanks for cutting me a deal, here's the six cups of flour."
msgstr "Gracias por hacer un trato, aquí están las seis tazas de harina."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "Thanks, but I think I'll pass.  I gotta run."
msgstr "Gracias, pero creo que voy a pasar. Tengo que correr."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "Thanks, can we talk about something else?"
msgstr "Gracias, ¿podemos hablar de otra cosa?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "That sounds like a great deal, here's some flour for you."
msgstr "Eso suena muy bien, aquí tienes un poco de harina para ti."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"That's kind of you to say.  I'm doing my best to move on… it hurts, but in "
"the scale of things it could be worse.  Pablo and I still have each other, "
"that's a lot more than most."
msgstr ""
"Es muy amable de tu parte decir eso. Hago lo que puedo para seguir "
"adelante... me duele, pero en la escala de las cosas podría ser peor. Pablo "
"y yo todavía nos tenemos el uno al otro, eso es mucho más que la mayoría."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"Things are tense at the best of times.  We didn't choose this crowd, so not "
"all of us really get along.  I like Jenny and Fatima, and the three of us "
"are kind of lucky to have friends here, but that doesn't make up for us "
"being a bunch of unfamiliar faces crammed into a tiny space.  Someone's "
"gonna murder someone soon, mark my words."
msgstr ""
"Las cosas están tensas en el mejor de los casos. No elegimos esta multitud, "
"así que no todos nos llevamos bien. Me gustan Jenny y Fátima, y las tres "
"tenemos la suerte de tener amigos aquí, pero eso no compensa el hecho de que "
"seamos un montón de caras desconocidas apiñadas en un espacio diminuto. "
"Alguien va a asesinar a alguien pronto, recuerda mis palabras."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Dana's family sourdough culture"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "This ain't it."
msgstr "No es esto."

#. ~ Description of "Dana's family sourdough starter"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"This crusty old jar has a glow-in-the-dark Millennium Falcon decal on the "
"side, and a label that reads, \"Landough Calrisean.  Dana's.  Do not touch "
"on pain of death\".  It's been abandoned for some time and doesn't look like "
"it could be readily salvaged as a sourdough culture, but maybe an "
"experienced sourdough baker could manage it."
msgstr ""
"Este tarro viejo tiene pegada una calcomanía del Halcón Milenario "
"fosforescente, y una etiqueta que dice \"Pan Solo\". De Dana. No tocar bajo "
"pena de muerte\". Hace mucho que está abandonado y no parece como si pudiera "
"recuperarse como masa cultivada, pero tal vez un panadero experimentado "
"pueda salvarla."

#. ~ Description of "Dana's sourdough bread"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"This round loaf of bread has a thick, dark crust, and smells very enticing."
msgstr ""
"Este pan redondo tiene una corteza gruesa y oscura, y huele muy "
"sugerentemente."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "Why not?  I'll see what I can do."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "You know, I think I changed my mind.  Can we talk about something else?"
msgstr "Sabes, creo que he cambiado de opinión. ¿Podemos hablar de otra cosa?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"You seem pretty unhappy about the quality of your bread.  Is there something "
"I can do to help?"
msgstr ""
"Pareces bastante infeliz por la calidad de tu pan. ¿Hay algo que pueda hacer "
"para ayudarte?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"Your husband said to ask you what you'd think about getting out of this "
"place and coming to work for me at my own camp."
msgstr ""
"Tu esposo me dijo que te preguntara qué pensarías de salir de este lugar y "
"venir a trabajar para mí en mi propio campamento."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "[1 merch] All right, one merch as agreed."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid "[2 merch] I got two merch for you."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"[BARTER] Aw, c'mon.  I rescued Landough, can't you cut me a little deal?"
msgstr ""
"[TRUEQUE] Aw, c'mon. He rescatado a Landough, ¿no puedes hacer un pequeño "
"trato?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
msgid ""
"[BARTER] Is that the lowest you can go?  I'd love some bread, but I can't "
"quite make that."
msgstr ""
"[TRUEQUE] ¿Es lo más bajo que puedes llegar? Me encantaría un poco de pan, "
"pero no puedo hacerlo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"\"We were… I… we can scarcely remember those times.\"  Dave looks pained.  "
"\"No, we had no doctor.  We didn't need one.  We had a job and… and… we "
"don't like to talk about this.\""
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"*gestures about his new home.  \"We have everything we wanted.  They cannot "
"see us here, and our mind is at peace.  We go outside as we need, and the "
"safety we have received here stays with us, as long as we are careful about "
"it.  In time, perhaps we will again have need of your noble services.\""
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"*nods deeply.  \"We are, for where we once were in chaos, now we are at "
"peace.  In time, this shall bring wisdom, but we must ponder on these great "
"changes.\""
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"*sits in a surprisingly well-built room made of lovingly assembled cardboard "
"boxes.  The area is quite clean and cozy.  The whole building is built on "
"top of cargo pallets, insulated with scraps, and waterproofed with plastic.  "
"It shows an unexpected amount of design prowess.  \"Hello, my noble knight "
"errant,\" Dave intones, his voice solemn.  \"We owe you a great debt for "
"your actions of the past.  Some day, we shall repay it.  Until then, you are "
"welcome here, now and always.\""
msgstr ""
"*se siente en una habitación sorprendentemente bien construida hecha con "
"cajas de cartón hermosamente ensambladas. El lugar está bastante limpio y es "
"cómodo. Todo el edificio está construido con palés, aislado con chatarra e "
"impermeabilizado con plástico. Demuestra una cantidad inesperada de destreza "
"en diseño. \"Hola, mi noble caballero errante,\" recita Dave con voz "
"solemne. \"Te debemos mucho por tus acciones del pasado. Algún día, "
"deberemos pagarte. Hasta entonces, sos bienvenido acá, ahora y siempre.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"*winces.  \"It is true.  You have earned some truth, but we… we find it hard "
"to give.  We had a job, an education.  Prestige.  It is all very faint now."
"\"  He touches a stainless steel ring on his pinky finger, looking lost in "
"thought.  \"We don't know why that man left, and this one remains.  Perhaps "
"that is some wisdom that will come with time, or perhaps it is a door best "
"left closed.\""
msgstr ""
"*hace un gesto de dolor. \"Es verdad. Te ganaste mi honestidad pero… nos "
"cuesta serlo. Teníamos un trabajo, una educación. Prestigio. Ahora todo es "
"muy distante.\" Toca un anillo de acero inoxidable que tiene en su meñique, "
"perdido en sus pensamientos. \"No sabes por qué se fue ese hombre y este se "
"quedó. Tal vez será una sabiduría que llegará con el tiempo, o tal vez es "
"una puerta que es mejor dejar cerrada.\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Always good to catch up, Dave.  Keep on being you."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Come on, Dave.  We're friends.  I won't use this against you or anything."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Hi Dave.  You seem different."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "How are things going up here on the roof?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
msgid ""
"Were you like this, uh, before?  Did you use to have a doctor or anything?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "You seem different."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
msgid "Ah yes, that's the spirit!  This place could sure use more dancing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
