msgstr "Leñador"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
msgid ""
"The rate is a bit steep, but I still have my quotas that I need to fulfill.  "
"The logs will be dropped off in the garage at the entrance to the camp.  "
"I'll need a bit of time before I can deliver another load."
msgstr ""
"El precio es un poco alto pero todavía tengo que cumplir con mi cuota. Los "
"leños serán dejados en en el garage a la entrada del campamento. Necesito un "
"poco de tiempo antes de que pueda entregar otra carga."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
msgid "You need something?"
msgstr "¿Necesitas algo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
msgid "[4800 merch, 7d] 100 logs"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
msgid "[800 merch, 1d] 10 logs"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter2.json
msgid ""
"Bringing in logs is one of the few tasks we can give to the unskilled, so "
"I'd be hurting them if I outsourced it.  Ask around though, I'm sure most "
"people could use a hand."
msgstr ""
"Traer leños es una de las pocas tareas que podemos darles a los que no "
"tienen habilidades, así que estaría perjudicándolos si subcontrato la tarea. "
"Igual, preguntá por ahí, seguro que la mayoría de la gente necesita una mano."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter2.json
msgid "Don't have much time to talk."
msgstr "No tengo mucho tiempo para hablar."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter2.json
msgid ""
"I turn the logs that laborers bring in into lumber to expand the outpost.  "
"Maintaining the saw is a chore, but breaks the monotony."
msgstr ""
"Convierto en madera los leños que traen los trabajadores para expandir el "
"puesto. El mantenimiento de la sierra es un embole pero rompe la monotonía."

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Flavor
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter2.json
msgid "Woodworker"
msgstr "Carpintero"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid ""
"*shrugs.  \"We got our hands on a few boxes of test strips so that's good.  "
"Being stressed isn't good for conception and I've been pretty fuckin' "
"stressed for a while.  I like our chances a lot better now, that's for "
"sure.  And, well, we've got our own private space at least.\"  She smirks "
"and then blushes slightly, hiding it by fiddling with her baking project."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid ""
"*sighs and nods.  \"Making do with what I've got, but yeah.  I can only "
"crank out a couple loaves a day, and can't do anything fun.  Pablo has been "
"talking about setting me up a separate kitchen to really get going, but "
"we've got so much critical work to do, and fresh bread is a luxury, even if "
"it's great for morale.\""
msgstr ""
"*suspira y asiente. \"Haciendo lo que puedo con lo que tengo, pero sí. Solo "
"puedo hacer un par de panes al día y no puedo hacer nada divertido. Pablo ha "
"estado hablando de prepararme una cocina separada para realmente ponerme en "
"marcha, pero tenemos tanto trabajo crítico que hacer y el pan fresco es un "
"lujo, aunque sería ¡genial! para levantar el ánimo.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid ""
"*stands in the middle of a cramped kitchen, covered in flour.  The scene "
"looks reminiscent of easier times, but the illusion is broken as he apron "
"shifts to reveal a heavy machete and holstered pistol on  her belt.  She "
"looks up as you approach, then beams in recognition.  \"Welcome to Dana's "
"Bakery, stranger!\"  She laughs brightly.  \"Glad you made out this way.  "
"What can I do for you?\""
msgstr ""
"*se encuentra en medio de una cocina abarrotada, cubierto de harina. La "
"escena parece evocar tiempos más fáciles, pero la ilusión se rompe cuando su "
"delantal se desplaza para revelar un pesado machete y una pistola enfundada "
"en su cinturón. Ella levanta la vista cuando te acercas, luego sonríe al "
"reconocerte. \"¡Bienvenido a la Panadería de Dana, desconocido!\" Ríe "
"brillantemente. \"Me alegra que hayas llegado hasta aquí. ¿En qué puedo "
"ayudarte?\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
